<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">fold-anchor</ansi> spell

<ansi fg="white-bold">Fold Anchor</ansi> lets you mark a location and teleport back to it later.
The spell has two modes depending on whether you have an anchor set:

  <ansi fg="yellow">No anchor set (or standing on your anchor):</ansi>
  Sets a Chrysalis anchor at your current location. The anchor persists
  until you set a new one somewhere else.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Anchor set and you are elsewhere:</ansi>
  Folds the Veil and teleports you back to your anchor point.

You can only have one anchor at a time. Casting the spell while standing
on your existing anchor refreshes it. Casting from anywhere else recalls
you to it.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast fold-anchor</ansi>     Set anchor or recall to it.

<ansi fg="yellow">Base Folds:  </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">6</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Target:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Self</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Conv. Cost:  </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">50</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Enhancement</ansi>

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help cast</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help spells</ansi>
